A||||7||BurlyGoat||Master Cylinder||||1||
Z||000000||BurlyGoat||09-09-2001||08:16 PM||||I have an 86 se V6 that I have just done the brake lines. When I hit the Brake (after bleeding it) the brake fluid goes about a foot into the air above the master cylinder. Does this mean the Master Cylinder is bad ?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||09-09-2001||08:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BurlyGoat:<BR><B>I have an 86 se V6 that I have just done the brake lines. When I hit the Brake (after bleeding it) the brake fluid goes about a foot into the air above the master cylinder. Does this mean the Master Cylinder is bad ?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||09-09-2001||08:50 PM||||Doesn't that mean you left the cap off the reservoir?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000003||theogre||09-09-2001||11:30 PM||||Did you do the pedal bleed method? Yes? Then yes, the MC could have died. Pedal bleeding can damage the MC if allot of crud settled in th bore.<P>Just as likely, you still have air in it.... Did the MC tank ever run dry durring bleeding? you could have air in the MC. read my brake service article.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BurlyGoat||09-10-2001||08:58 AM||||The master cylinder was dry to start with. Followed the brake instructions to a T and spent alot of time and fluid bleeding the brakes...Checked with several other cars in the driveway with the master cylinder cap off and non of them spewed brake fluid up like this....<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||SteveJ||09-10-2001||09:11 AM||||You still have air in the system. If not the MC then next most likely is the lines to the back.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-10-2001||07:35 PM||||At the very least the MC will have to be bench bled. You'll likely never get it on the car. A power or vac bleeder might get it but don't count on it.<P>If it still does this after bench bleeding then the MC is probably bad. Read the brake upgrade article in my cave for more info on how a stock Fiero MC works.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BurlyGoat||09-11-2001||02:48 PM||||Thanks for your help, I guess the MC is coming out...<P>||||reg||9
